    "overall": "Spain are clear favorites despite playing a friendly in Mexico, with a 68.3% average possession and 17.7 shots per game in recent stats compared to Peru's 50.2% possession and 8.4 shots. However, the breaking news that Lamine Yamal and Nico Williams have been left out of Spain's squad is significant—both are elite wingers who would have exploited Peru's defensive vulnerabilities. Spain still possess quality through Ferrán Torres, Mikel Oyarzabal, and Dani Olmo, plus Rodri and Fabián Ruiz to control midfield. Peru showed promise beating Haiti 2-1 and drawing Honduras 2-2, but struggled against Senegal (0-2) and have a much lower xG profile. Spain's expected goals per game in recent friendlies (3-0 vs Serbia, 1-1 vs Iraq) suggests they can score 2 goals even without their best wingers, while Peru's away-style attack will likely find the net once against a rotated Spain backline. The neutral venue in Puebla somewhat evens the home advantage, but Spain's technical superiority and squad depth should still prevail. I project Spain winning around 55-60% of scenarios, with Peru competitive in 15-20% and draws at 20-25%.",
